cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RelyFetal: Reliability-aware single-channel fetal QRS detection"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ngo"
    given-names: "Binh Minh"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information Technology, Ton Duc Thang University"
    city: "Ho Chi Minh City"
    country: "VN"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bminhnemhoi/nckhsv_tdtu2026-2027"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline for detecting fetal QRS complexes from single-channel
  abdominal electrocardiography, with the experimental evidence behind every
  design decision and every retraction recorded in place. A 113,481-parameter
  dilated temporal convolutional network reaches 97.56 macro F1 over 22
  independent women (label-blind lead), against 98.83 for the four-lead Power-MF
  pipeline re-run locally and 86.71 for Power-MF restricted to one lead. On the
  60 CinC 2013 set-a records that are not copies of the training data (the
  overlap was documented by the Challenge organisers; we identified the 15
  records by measurement) the label-blind score is 74.28. The proposed
  persistent-homology signal-quality index is reported as a negative result
  (AUROC 0.566 vs 0.929 for classical indices); a classical reject gate is kept.
keywords:
  - fetal electrocardiography
  - fetal QRS detection
  - single-channel source separation
  - temporal convolutional network
  - signal quality index
  - persistent homology
  - topological data analysis
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
